        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Seville</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 750 BCE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">Its original core dates to the 8th century BCE, when the town stood on an island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadalquivir">Guadalquivir</a>. By myth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hercules-kassel">Hercules</a>, identified with the Phoenician god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/melqart">Melqart</a>, founded it; the Tartessians called it Spal or Ispal, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> Latinised the name as Hispalis.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the lower reaches of the River <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadalquivir">Guadalquivir</a> in the south-west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberian Peninsula</a>, about 80 km from the Atlantic, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andalusia">Andalusia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">Roman Hispalis; the Visigothic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> Leander and Isidore; the capital of the Abbadid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> capital with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giralda">Giralda</a> and the Torre del Oro; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/casa-de-contratacion">Casa de Contratación</a> and the monopoly of the American trade; the plague of 1649; the painters Velázquez, Murillo and Zurbarán; the Ibero-American Exposition of 1929 and Expo '92</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Seville is the capital of the autonomous community of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andalusia">Andalusia</a> and of the province of Seville, and the fifth-largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>.</span></div>
